1. 飲茶
廣東話：我哋聽朝去飲茶，順便傾下個project嘅嘢。
English: We'll go for dim sum tomorrow morning and talk about the project at the same time.

2. 圖書館
廣東話：佢成日去圖書館溫書，貪嗰度夠靜。
English: He often goes to the library to study because it's quiet there.

3. 養聲
廣東話：你把聲沙晒，快啲飲啲蜜糖水養聲啦。
English: Your voice is hoarse, drink some honey water to soothe your throat.

4. 票尾
廣東話：張戲飛嘅票尾唔好掉，可以留返嚟做紀念。
English: Don't throw away the ticket stub, you can keep it as a souvenir.

5. hacker
廣東話：有個hacker試圖入侵我哋公司嘅伺服器。
English: A hacker tried to break into our company's server.

6. 石斛蘭
廣東話：呢棵石斛蘭開花好靚，佢係依附喺棵樹上面生長嘅。
English: This dendrobium orchid is blooming beautifully; it grows attached to a tree.

7. 吊詭
廣東話：呢件事聽落好吊詭，明明係壞事但係又有人讚。
English: This sounds very paradoxical—it's clearly a bad thing, yet some people praise it.

8. 吊詭
廣東話：佢嘅說法吊詭到令人難以置信。
English: His statement is so absurd that it's hard to believe.

9. 各為其主
廣東話：兩隊波嘅球員各為其主，喺場上拼盡全力。
English: The players of both teams fight for their own side, giving their all on the pitch.

10. 軨蓋
廣東話：我架車個軨蓋唔見咗，要去車房配返個。
English: I lost the wheel cover on my car; I need to get a replacement at the garage.

11. 打哥夫
廣東話：老細今日唔返工，話要去打哥夫喎。
English: The boss isn't coming to work today; he said he's going to play golf.

12. 免揀
廣東話：呢啲生果係免揀嘅，唔該你哋唔好逐個揀。
English: These fruits are not for picking—please don't pick through them one by one.

13. 擺闊佬
廣東話：佢成日喺朋友面前擺闊佬，爭住埋單。
English: He always shows off his wealth in front of friends, insisting on paying the bill.

14. 廣播劇
廣東話：我細個好鍾意聽收音機嘅廣播劇。
English: When I was young, I really loved listening to radio dramas.

15. 錄影機
廣東話：屋企部錄影機壞咗，而家啲人淨係用電話錄影。
English: The video recorder at home is broken; nowadays people just record with their phones.

16. 吟詩吟唔甩
廣東話：今次俾人捉到正，吟詩吟唔甩喇。
English: This time he was caught red-handed; there's no way he can talk his way out of it.

17. 佈道大會
廣東話：教會今個禮拜搞佈道大會，歡迎大家參加。
English: The church is holding an evangelistic rally this week; everyone is welcome to join.

18. 寫手
廣東話：佢係一個出色嘅寫手，幫唔少雜誌寫專欄。
English: He is an excellent writer who writes columns for many magazines.

19. 寫手
廣東話：呢位明星嘅自傳其實係由代筆寫手操刀。
English: This celebrity's autobiography was actually ghostwritten by a ghostwriter.

20. 代打
廣東話：我個fd叫我幫佢代打幾鋪機。
English: My friend asked me to play a few rounds of the game for him.

21. 茶碗
廣東話：呢隻茶碗係日本茶道用嘅，手工好精緻。
English: This tea bowl is used in Japanese tea ceremony; the craftsmanship is exquisite.

22. 茶隔
廣東話：沖普洱茶記得用茶隔隔住啲茶葉，唔係飲落去好嚡。
English: Remember to use a tea strainer when brewing pu'er tea, otherwise it feels rough when you drink it.

23. 只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈
廣東話：佢自己遲到就得，我遲到就俾人鬧，真係只許州官放火，不准百姓點燈。
English: He can be late himself, but when I'm late I get scolded—it's really a case of double standards.

24. 獨唱
廣東話：今晚個音樂會佢會獨唱一首歌，冇人伴唱。
English: At tonight's concert, she will sing a solo without anyone accompanying her.

25. 快人快事
廣東話：佢不嬲快人快事，應承咗就即刻去做。
English: He's always quick to act—once he agrees, he gets it done right away.

26. 四腳獸
廣東話：有人話喺公園個廁所見到四腳獸，真係嚇死人。
English: Someone said they saw a "four-legged beast" in the park toilet—that's really scary.

27. 無米粥
廣東話：呢單生意仲係煲無米粥，細節都未傾好。
English: This deal is still in the early talking stage; the details haven't been discussed yet.

28. 義會
廣東話：舊時啲街坊會搞義會，等有急需嘅人可以借錢周轉。
English: In the old days, neighbors would organize a rotating credit association so people in urgent need could borrow money.

29. 榜文
廣東話：古代衙門前面會貼榜文，公告重要嘅事。
English: In ancient times, notices would be posted in front of the government office to announce important matters.

30. MK名
廣東話：佢個MK名加咗好多符號，睇到人一頭霧水。
English: His MK-style username has so many symbols that it's completely confusing. [end of text]


